  "title": "Sharpeville massacre survivors demand justice in South Africa",
  "summary": "Sharpeville massacre survivors are seeking justice for the 1960 attack on protesters, with victims demanding compensation for years of suffering. The case highlights ongoing struggles for justice after decades of apartheid.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "At least 69 people were shot dead in 1960 in the Sharpeville massacre.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "No one has been prosecuted for the attack, and victims want restitution.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The attack occurred on 21 March 1960 and was part of a wave of litigation over apartheid crimes in South Africa.",
